      "text": "To find the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two 6-sided dice is a prime number, we need to:\n\n1. Determine all possible outcomes when two dice are rolled.\n2. Identify the sums that are prime numbers.\n3. Calculate the probability by dividing the number of favorable outcomes by the total number of outcomes.\n\n**Step 1: Determine all possible outcomes**\n\nEach die has 6 faces, so there are \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\) possible outcomes when two dice are rolled.\n\n**Step 2: Identify the sums that are prime numbers**\n\nThe possible sums of the numbers on two dice range from 2 to 12. The prime numbers in this range are 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11.\n\n**Step 3: Count the number of favorable outcomes**\n\nWe will count the number of ways to get each of these prime sums:\n\n- **Sum = 2**: (1, 1) -- 1 way\n- **Sum = 3**: (1, 2), (2, 1) -- 2 ways\n- **Sum = 5**: (1, 4), (2, 3), (3, 2), (4, 1) -- 4 ways\n- **Sum = 7**: (1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4), (4, 3), (5, 2), (6, 1) -- 6 ways\n- **Sum = 11**: (5, 6), (6, 5) -- 2 ways\n\nAdding these together, the total number of favorable outcomes is:\n\\[1 + 2 + 4 + 6 + 2 = 15\\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the probability**\n\nThe probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12}\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\\).",
