      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two standard 6-sided dice is a prime number. We will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of possible outcomes:**\n   Each die has 6 faces, so when two dice are tossed, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 6 = 36\n   \\]\n\n2. **List all possible sums of the numbers on the dice:**\n   The minimum sum occurs when both dice show 1:\n   \\[\n   1 + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   The maximum sum occurs when both dice show 6:\n   \\[\n   6 + 6 = 12\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the possible sums range from 2 to 12.\n\n3. **Identify the prime numbers in this range:**\n   The prime numbers between 2 and 12 are:\n   \\[\n   2, 3, 5, 7, 11\n   \\]\n\n4. **Count the number of ways to achieve each prime sum:**\n   - **Sum = 2:**\n     \\[\n     (1, 1) \\quad \\text{(1 way)}\n     \\]\n   - **Sum = 3:**\n     \\[\n     (1, 2), (2, 1) \\quad \\text{(2 ways)}\n     \\]\n   - **Sum = 5:**\n     \\[\n     (1, 4), (2, 3), (3, 2), (4, 1) \\quad \\text{(4 ways)}\n     \\]\n   - **Sum = 7:**\n     \\[\n     (1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4), (4, 3), (5, 2), (6, 1) \\quad \\text{(6 ways)}\n     \\]\n   - **Sum = 11:**\n     \\[\n     (5, 6), (6, 5) \\quad \\text{(2 ways)}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Summarize the number of ways to achieve each prime sum:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{aligned}\n   &2 \\text{ ways}, \\\\\n   &3 \\text{ ways}, \\\\\n   &5 \\text{ ways}, \\\\\n   &6 \\text{ ways}, \\\\\n   &2 \\text{ ways}.\n   \\end{aligned}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the total number of favorable outcomes:**\n   \\[\n   1 + 2 + 4 + 6 + 2 = 15\n   \\]\n\n7. **Determine the probability:**\n   The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15}{36}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Simplify the fraction:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\n\\]",
