    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on two standard 6-sided dice is a prime number, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of possible outcomes:**\n   Each die has 6 faces, so when two dice are tossed, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 6 = 36\n   \\]\n\n2. **List all possible sums and check which are prime:**\n   The possible sums range from \\(2\\) to \\(12\\). We need to identify which of these sums are prime numbers. The prime numbers in this range are:\n   \\[\n   2, 3, 5, 7, 11\n   \\]\n\n3. **Count the number of ways to achieve each prime sum:**\n   - **Sum = 2:** The only way to get a sum of 2 is \\(1 + 1\\). There is 1 way.\n   - **Sum = 3:** The ways to get a sum of 3 are \\(1 + 2\\) and \\(2 + 1\\). There are 2 ways.\n   - **Sum = 5:** The ways to get a sum of 5 are \\(1 + 4\\), \\(2 + 3\\), \\(3 + 2\\), and \\(4 + 1\\). There are 4 ways.\n   - **Sum = 7:** The ways to get a sum of 7 are \\(1 + 6\\), \\(2 + 5\\), \\(3 + 4\\), \\(4 + 3\\), \\(5 + 2\\), and \\(6 + 1\\). There are 6 ways.\n   - **Sum = 11:** The ways to get a sum of 11 are \\(5 + 6\\) and \\(6 + 5\\). There are 2 ways.\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of favorable outcomes:**\n   The total number of ways to get a prime sum is the sum of the ways to get each prime sum:\n   \\[\n   1 + 2 + 4 + 6 + 2 = 15\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine the probability:**\n   The probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the sum of the numbers shown on the dice is a prime number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\n\\]",
